{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Johnson. I'm Dr. Patel, one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in with chest pain. Can you tell me more about what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. I was playing dominos yesterday when I suddenly got a sharp pain in the middle of my chest. It hurts more when I breathe deeply."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Was the pain radiating anywhere, like your arm or jaw?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it stayed right in the center. I took a nitroglycerin tablet, but it didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any shortness of breath or cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been coughing a little and it’s harder to catch my breath, especially when I walk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history of pulmonary embolism and being on warfarin, we needed to check if this could be another clot in your lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s what I was worried about. My last one was really scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CT scan of your chest to look for that. The good news is there’s no new large clot. But there are small clots that appear to be resolving from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a new PE? But why does my chest hurt so much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pain is likely from irritation in the lining of your lungs due to the old clots healing. That’s why it gets worse when you breathe deeply."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. But I thought my blood was thin enough. I’ve been taking warfarin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR came back at 1.4 when you arrived, which is below the target range. That means your blood wasn’t thin enough to prevent clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m still at risk even though I’m on the medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s why we’ve started you on a faster-acting blood thinner called enoxaparin, also known as Lovenox. It will work while we adjust your warfarin dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll have to give myself shots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice a day for about two weeks. A nurse will teach you how, or your daughter can help if you’re comfortable with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "She’s coming later. That might be easier at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. We also checked your heart enzymes and did an EKG. Everything looks stable, so this doesn’t appear to be heart-related chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. My dad had heart attacks young, so I always worry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But your heart function is stable, and your ejection fraction is still around 55%, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my diabetes and thyroid? I noticed you held my metformin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We usually hold metformin in the hospital because of the risk of kidney issues, especially with contrast from scans. But you’re back on it now, and your blood sugars have been okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2192-07-27 16:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin? I’ve been checking my levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on your usual insulin doses. We’ve been monitoring your glucose, and it’s been in a safe range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want to have any complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re keeping a close eye on everything. Your other medications like aspirin, atorvastatin, and blood pressure pills are continuing as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been coughing a lot. Is that from the PE too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be. The healing process can irritate the lungs. We’ve given you a mild cough suppressant with codeine to help at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I haven’t been sleeping well because of the cough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2192-07-27 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad we can help with that. Your breathing sounds are clear, and oxygen levels are normal, so that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Johnson. I’m here to update you. Your repeat labs look stable, and you’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Does that mean I’m out of danger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The immediate risk is low. The clots are getting smaller, and with the new Lovenox and adjusted warfarin, we’re making sure your blood stays thin enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You said something about an INR check?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You need to get your INR checked at the clinic on Thursday. It’s important to make sure it’s in the right range before we stop the Lovenox."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll go. My daughter will take me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Also, keep taking the oxycodone for pain as needed, but it should improve over the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the chest pain gets worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have sudden shortness of breath, chest pressure, or cough up blood, go to the ER immediately. Otherwise, call your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, doctor. I feel much better knowing what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2192-07-28 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready, and a nurse will go over your medications before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick final check before you go. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Only a little sore when I take a deep breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Keep using your walker if you need it, especially when you’re tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I don’t want to fall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smart. And remember, follow up with your primary doctor and take that INR test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve already written it down. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2192-07-28 16:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it, doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2192-07-27 16:36:00",
    "admission_end": "2192-07-28 17:09:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old man with a history of coronary artery disease, diabetes, hypertension, and prior pulmonary embolism on warfarin presented with pleuritic chest pain, cough, and shortness of breath. He was subtherapeutic on admission with an INR of 1.4. A CT angiogram showed minimal partially occlusive filling defects consistent with resolving pulmonary emboli and no acute clot. Cardiac enzymes were negative, and the pain was attributed to pleural irritation from healing clots. He was started on a heparin drip and transitioned to enoxaparin for bridging while adjusting warfarin. His chronic conditions remained stable, and he was discharged home with instructions to continue anticoagulation, monitor for worsening symptoms, and obtain an INR check in clinic.",
    "problems": [
      "Other pulmonary embolism and infarction",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
